          "price": "price",
          "avg_rating_meta": "average_rating",
          "rating_count_meta": "rating_number",
          "details": "details",
          "seller": null
        },
        "required": [
          "item_id"
        ]
      },
      "notes": {
        "brand_is_store": "Amazon Reviews 2023 has NO `brand` field. `store` is the Amazon storefront name, which usually but not always coincides with the manufacturer. We map store -> brand and label the graph node type `Brand (proxy: store)`. This is an approximation and is reported as such; it is not a ground-truth brand.\n",
        "seller_absent": "There is NO seller field. Per the project rule against inventing entities, the heterogeneous graph therefore has NO Seller node type and no `sold_by` edge. The architecture diagram must reflect this.\n",
        "categories_sparse": "`categories` is an empty list for a large share of products. `main_category` is far better populated. The Category node type is built primarily from main_category, with the `categories` leaf used only when non-empty.\n",
        "price_sparse": "`price` is null for a large share of products and is a string in some rows. Price is treated as an optional feature with an explicit missingness indicator, never imputed silently.\n",
        "no_fraud_labels": "There are NO fake-review or fraud labels. Trust scores from Module 11/12 are therefore UNSUPERVISED and cannot be scored against ground truth. Evaluation uses synthetic injection experiments (Module 45), which must always be reported as synthetic.\n"
      }
    },
